# Large data files must NOT be committed to git.
#
# GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100 MB, and git keeps every version
# forever — a large file committed once bloats the repo permanently, even
# if deleted later. Raw reads and reference databases are GB-scale, so
# they are fetched on demand by download_data.sh instead.
#
# Anything genuinely needed in-repo (small demo subsamples, metadata,
# manifests) is force-added and listed under "Tracked exceptions" below.

raw/
references/
taxonomy/

# Common sequence + archive formats, wherever they appear
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.fasta
*.fa
*.fna
*.sra
*.gz
*.zip
*.tar
*.dmp

# --- Tracked exceptions -----------------------------------------------
# Small, committed-on-purpose files that the patterns above would catch.
!samples/**
!metadata/**
!.gitignore
